---
title: Kleftiko v2
source: https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/wordofmouth/2016/aug/18/how-to-cook-the-perfect-kleftiko
servings: 6
prep time: 30m
cook time: 5h15m
course: Main
locale: en
difficulty: Medium
cuisine: Greek
---

Roughly crush @garlic{0.5%head} and rub over the @lamb shoulder{2%kg}. Pour the @olive oil{} and @lemon juice{2%tbsp} over the meat, and sprinkle with the @ground cinnamon{1%tsp}, @dried oregano{1%tsp}, and @salt{1%tsp}. Rub all of the ingredients into the meat and leave for ~{12%hours}.

Heat oven to 160°C.

Place two pieces of greaseproof paper at right-angles into the base of a roasting pan, large enough to fold over the top of the joint. Use a roasting pan that is shorter than the paper width so that the liquid will be contained when wrapped.

Line the base of the roasting tin with the @waxy potatoes{1%kg}(cut into wedges), @red onion{1%large}(cut into wedges), @red pepper{1}(cut into chunky strips), and @cherry tomatoes{12}. Add the @bay leaf{1}, and the @garlic{1%head}(cut in half laterally). Squeeze the @lemon{1} over the vegetables and add its shells. Pour @water{200%ml} into the dish.

Place the lamb shoulder on top of the vegetables. Sprinkle the overhanging greaseproof paper with water and fold over to form a sealed package.

Bake for 4 to ~{5%hours} until very tender.

Turn the oven up to 200°C and roast uncovered for 10 to ~{15%minutes}.

Remove the lamb shoulder and set aside. Roast the vegetables for a further 15 minutes until starting to brown, then serve with the meat.